{"id": "EUVD-2026-108318", "enisaUuid": "6fbc128a-1b14-3510-82c5-d7c0670f71bf", "description": "wasmtime-wasi-http in Wasmtime before 36.0.16, 37.0.0 before 48.0.3, and 49.0.0 before 49.0.1 does not enforce the wasi:io/streams check-write allowance for WASIp2 outgoing HTTP bodies, so oversized writes succeed instead of trapping. A malicious guest can pass large buffers to write on outgoing-body resources, holding host allocations for the store's lifetime and exhausting host memory.", "datePublished": "2026-10-22T19:13:54", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-22T19:13:54", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/security/advisories/GHSA-c9gc-w9vx-w86p", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/wasmtime-before-36.0.16-37.0.0-before-48.0.3-and-49.0.0-before-49.0.1-memory-exhaustion-dos-via-wasmtime-wasi-http-outgoing-body-write"], "aliases": ["GHSA-7qg7-h7wh-p6q8", "CVE-2026-115388"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "7bc552ef-c0d9-32e5-8fd7-941fcd033abf", "product": {"name": "wasmtime", "vendor": {"name": "bytecodealliance"}}, "product_version": "37.0.0 <48.0.3"}, {"id": "9c399442-6193-339b-bc96-ff2c755cb985", "product": {"name": "wasmtime", "vendor": {"name": "bytecodealliance"}}, "product_version": "0 <36.0.16"}, {"id": "fc68193e-33d5-38b0-bcd2-885ddc5bedcd", "product": {"name": "wasmtime", "vendor": {"name": "bytecodealliance"}}, "product_version": "49.0.0 <49.0.1"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "8dbebce7-fef1-367f-8233-196cd438c5d0", "vendor": {"name": "bytecodealliance"}}], "isExploited": false}